Package: spatbiome
Title: A Nonparametric Test for Co-Clustering in Spatial Microbiome Data
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R:
    person("Asmita", "Roy", , "aroy38@jh.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements Area-adjusted Random Shift, a non-parametric test to assess co-clustering of two point patterns. The two point processes are assumed to be independently superimposed under the null hypothesis. The test is based on Ripley's bivariate K-function and uses random shifts of one of the point patterns to generate a null distribution. An area-adjusted scale factor stabilises the variance across random shifts.
Imports:
    GET,
    future,
    future.apply,
    parallel,
    spatstat.explore,
    spatstat.geom,
    spatstat.random
